{"ld": 1120, "paper": "HP739", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Promote the Secure Storage of Firearms", "sponsor_id": "h-sayre-daniel", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-abdi-mana", "h-ankeles-daniel", "s-carney-anne", "h-cloutier-kristen", "h-doudera-victoria", "h-gramlich-lori", "h-roeder-amy"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "Under current law, it is a Class D crime to negligently store a loaded firearm in a manner that allows a child under 16 years of age to gain access to the loaded firearm without the permission of the child's parent. This bill repeals that law and makes it a Class D crime to negligently store a firearm so that a minor or person who is prohibited from possessing a firearm may gain access to the firearm and either use it in the commission of a crime or display it in a threatening manner. The bill also makes it a Class C crime to negligently store a firearm in a way so that a minor or prohibited person may gain access to the firearm and use it to cause the death of or serious bodily injury to any person. The bill also requires licensed firearms dealers to post a notice in any area where sales or transfers occur informing purchasers that access to a firearm in the home significantly increases the risk of suicide, death during domestic violence disputes and unintentional death of children.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0739&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Accepted Minority (ONTP) Report", "final_disposition": {"label": "Accepted Minority (ONTP) Report", "date": "2025-06-13", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1120)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0739&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-655)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP073